COLOSSEUM OVERHAUL 3.3.8

COMBINED RELEASE - GENERATIONS 1, 2 AND 3

3.3.8 fixes Gen 1 doubles preparation after deployment and Ruby/Sapphire Spikes dialogue on older native hosts. Camera framing uses direct trainer-height and manual-state reads to reduce temporary allocations. Existing features, diagnostics, source assets and cache formats are retained.

Idle Pokemon and trainer loops keep their natural real-time pace at higher battle speeds, including resting partners during moves. Source moves, trainer actions, faint-return and capture still follow the native game speed or the Colosseum battle speed setting. Opposing trainers retain their defeat pose during ending dialogue while the camera moves gently around the speaker. Pyrite boundaries and two-trainer framing are retained.

Outdoor foliage, hanging banners and cherry blossoms have stronger wind. Lightweight depth-tested outdoor atmosphere uses one static GPU batch; solid scenery, source assets and existing caches are retained.

Fixes missing enemy Pokemon during Gen 3 doubles deployment. Native reveal and ball-opening events are delivered once even when rendered frames are irregular or battle tempo is accelerated. Existing cleanup, presentation, models and cache compatibility are retained.

Adds CHERRY BLOSSOM GROVE: tall flowering trees, layered pink canopies, stone garden lanterns, moss, fallen blossoms and drifting 3D petals. Choose ARENA in the Colosseum battle settings. This original venue is included in the package and uses existing battle effects, models and camera controls across all three generations. The 3.0.1 starter animation correction is retained.

Colosseum arenas, 386 Pokemon models/portraits, source trainer actors, Waza arena effects/audio, battle camera, doubles, HD battle UI, dialogue/menus, Gen 3 level-up stats, Colosseum Dex, expanded encounters, move preparation, optional EXP Share and Mt. Battle.

INSTALL
Import this ZIP through the launcher, replace the previous combined package and enable one copy. Keep your Pokemon Colosseum USA import and generated caches; no global wipe is required. Reopen Mt. Battle after updating. Ruby/Sapphire require a Gen1Recomp release with native support. No ROMs, disc images, saves or generated caches are included.

MT. BATTLE
Gen 1/2: START > BATTLE > MT. BATTLE. Gen 3: START > COLOSSEUM > MT. BATTLE. Shared setup/music, climb formats, party/PC/all-386 rentals, custom teams and suspend/resume are retained. Challenges are available before the Elite Four with progression-independent obedience.

PERFORMANCE AND COMPATIBILITY
All existing features, source assets and cache identities are retained. Frame-based camera/presentation, reusable source lookups, preparation of linked particle tracks, mobile arena memory budgets and resize/rotation cleanup remain included. Development files and release history are excluded from this package. See README.md for controls, installation and verification scope. Third-party licenses are included.
